course: dictionary
lesson: 11364
title: Abandonment: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abandonment is a noun, a word for a thing that happens. It has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is right. «The kitten was found alone in a cardboard box, and its abandonment made everyone sad.» The kitten was left behind for ever by someone who should have cared for it.
explain: «The abandonment of the match came when the heavy rain started.» The match was stopped and not finished. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "stopping completely" in place of abandonment, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The third meaning is about wild, free behaviour. «The crowd danced with abandonment when the band began.» Here it means dancing freely, without holding back. This meaning is formal, so you will find it more in books than in everyday talk.
fact: Abandonment means leaving someone or something behind for ever, especially when you should have cared for them.
fact: «Abandonment» also means giving up a plan or activity completely, such as the abandonment of a match because of rain.
fact: In a formal sense, «abandonment» means acting wildly and freely, without control.
fact: Animal charities work hard to stop pet abandonment.
fact: In law, abandonment of a child or animal is a crime.
exercise: «The dog's abandonment made the whole street sad.» What does abandonment mean here? | A big party for the dog | *Leaving the dog behind for ever | Walking the dog every day | Giving the dog a bath
exercise: «The abandonment of the match came when the heavy rain started.» What happened to the match? | It was won by the team with the most goals | It was moved to a bigger pitch | It was played again the next day with no break | *It was stopped and not finished
exercise: «The crowd danced with abandonment when the band began.» What does abandonment mean here? | Dancing in a tidy line | *Dancing wildly and freely, without control | Dancing very slowly | Leaving the dance floor
test: Animal charities fight pet abandonment. Why do they fight it? | To teach pets to dance | *To stop people leaving pets behind for ever | To sell more pet food | To make pets go outside more
test: «Towns fell into ruin after their abandonment.» What does this suggest about abandonment? | The towns were made bigger | The towns were painted and made new | *People left the towns and did not return | The towns became famous for their tourists
exam: «After the abandonment, the old house stood empty for years.» What does abandonment mean in this sentence? | Adding a new room to the house | Painting the house a bright colour | *Leaving the house behind for ever | Cleaning the house before the guests come
